{
  "name": "forge_tarrasque",
  "_template": "Tarrasque archetype (exotic). A Gargantuan armoured biped: carapace-plated barrel, two forward-sweeping horns, a mouth that takes up most of the skull, small heavy forelimbs and a mace-thick tail. The pelvis/leg/foot geometry starts from the theropod archetype - that is the arrangement the balance gate already accepted (hips under the mass, long digitigrade foot) - and the tarrasque only adds weight above it. See _note_balance in joints for the one deliberate departure. Neutral slate-brown palette FOR tinting.",
  "palette": {
    "hide_body": { "color": "#7a7064", "rough": 0.95 },
    "hide_head": { "color": "#726859", "rough": 0.95 },
    "hide_tail": { "color": "#6d6457", "rough": 0.95 },
    "hide_leg": { "color": "#746a5d", "rough": 0.95 },
